me":false,"opp":"IU","oppName":"Indiana Hoosiers","result":"L","score":"27-13","values":[26,42,311,61.9,1,3,51,0,117.7,82.5,0,0,0,0,0]},{"id":"401858534","date":"2026-11-21","week":12,"type":"reg","home":true,"opp":"MD","oppName":"Maryland Terrapins","result":"W","score":"35-21","values":[21,35,237,60,2,0,32,0,135.7,77.7,1,12,12,0,12]}]}},"summaryLabel":"2026 season stats","news":[{"headline":"Betting on Ohio State-USC: How the Trojans can pull off the upset","description":"Could USC give the Buckeyes a good scare on Halloween? Let's dive into the numbers to find the best betting angle.","published":"2026-10-28T13:44:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50300744/college-football-betting-odds-week-9-ohio-state-usc-upset","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft QB rankings: Arch Manning, Dante Moore, Drew Mestemaker in top 15","description":"Who are the best quarterbacks in the 2027 draft class? We sized up the top 15, including Arch Manning, Dante Moore, Trinidad Chambliss and Darian Mensah.","published":"2026-10-09T12:14:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50117790/2027-nfl-draft-quarterbacks-ranking-strengths-weaknesses","type":"Story","byline":"Jordan Reid","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"'I'm not asking for anybody's sympathy': It's a pivotal season for Lincoln Riley and USC","description":"With a 4-0 record, Lincoln Riley isn't shying away from expectations as USC hosts Oregon this weekend.","published":"2026-09-24T22:04:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49713288/usc-lincoln-riley-hot-seat-job-security-2026","type":"Story","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"The oldest grudge in football","description":"When Texas Tech and its brash benefactor bought their way into the college football big time, they were settling an old West Texas score.","published":"2026-11-26T13:12:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50427039/texas-tech-puf-cody-campbell","type":"Story","byline":"Dave Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Take a 360-degree look at college football's iconic rivalry trophies","description":"Whether ancient, animal or absurd, college football's rivalry trophies take many shapes.","published":"2026-11-26T13:09:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/50371090/college-football-rivalry-trophies","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"USC band won't perform at UCLA football game after members vandalized campus","description":"The USC Trojan Marching Band will not perform during Saturday's rivalry game vs. UCLA after members of the band vandalized a portion of UCLA's campus.","published":"2026-11-26T04:37:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50600615/usc-band-perform-members-vandalized-ucla-campus","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Kent State TD overturned by replay was incorrect decision, MAC says","description":"A Kent State touchdown catch should not have been overturned by replay to incomplete at the end of Tuesday's 17-12 loss to Eastern Michigan, the Mid-American Conference said Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T23:05:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50597875/kent-state-td-overturned-replay-was-incorrect-mac-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-25T19:44:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Chris Creighton out as coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons","description":"Chris Creighton is out as head coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons with the school.","published":"2026-11-25T19:05:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50595706/creighton-coach-eastern-michigan-13-seasons","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge denies SEC's request for TRO against LSU in Dec. 3 vote","description":"A federal judge denied the SEC's request for a temporary restraining order to keep LSU from interfering with a Dec. 3 vote of presidents and chancellors on whether to remove the school from the conference.","published":"2026-11-25T20:02:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50595702/judge-denies-sec-request-tro-lsu-dec-3-vote","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4685454/jayden-maiava","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jayden_Maiava"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jayden Maiava","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jayden_Maiava","description":"American football player (born 2003)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:16Z","intro":"Jayden Ikaika Maiava  ( my-AH-vuh; born April 6, 2003) is an American college football quarterback for the USC Trojans. He previously played for the UNLV Rebels.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Maiava was born on April 6, 2003, in Honolulu, Hawa'ii."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"UNLV\nAfter redshirting in 2022, Maiava began the 2023 season as a backup. After an injury to Doug Brumfield against Vanderbilt, Maiava led UNLV to a comeback victory, throwing for 261 yards and combining for two touchdowns. The following week against UTEP, he made his first career start leading UNLV to a 45–28 victory. After finishing the regular season passing for 2,626 yards and 14 touchdowns, Maiava was named the Mountain West Freshman of the Year and to the all-conference second team. Following the conclusion of the regular season, he announced that he would be returning to UNLV the following season, despite speculation that he would transfer. However, Maiava went back on this decision on January 1, 2024, announcing that he would be entering the transfer portal.\n\nUSC\nOn January 8, 2024, Maiava announced that he would be transferring to the University of Georgia to play for the Georgia Bulldogs. However, the following day, he announced that he had flipped his commitment to the University of Southern California to play for the USC Trojans. Entering the 2024 season, Maiava was named as the backup to Miller Moss. After a 4–5 start to the season, Moss was benched, and Maiava was named the starter, becoming the first Polynesian quarterback to start at USC. In his first start with the Trojans against Nebraska, he threw for 249 yards and totaled four touchdowns, three passing and one rushing, leading USC to a 28–20 victory. In the 2024 Las Vegas Bowl, Maiava threw for 295 yards, four touchdowns, and three interceptions, leading the Trojans to a 35–31 comeback victory.\nMaiava led a strong start for the Trojans in 2025, piloting a 4–0 start to their season. USC suffered their first loss of the season against Illinois 34–32, where Maiava completed 30 of 43 passes for 364 yards, two touchdowns, both to wide receiver Makai Lemon, and one interception. Following a win against Michigan, Maiava and the trojans would fall short against rival Notre Dame, where he threw two touchdowns and two interceptions. After a win streak of three games, where Maiava compiled a total of 688 passing yards, three touchdowns and two interceptions, Maiava and the Trojans would fall to Oregon. USC would make an appearance in the Alamo Bowl, where they would lose in overtime to TCU 27–30. In 2025, Maiava finished the season with 3,711 passing yards with 24 touchdowns and 10 interceptions, and was a semifinalist for the Davey O'Brien Award."}],"family":[{"relation":"Relative","name":"Kaluka Maiava","description":"American football player","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaluka_Maiava"}]}}